# What the transport sends is what Berlinan's sends: tests/equiv/midi_full.midiscript (the full ensemble on its own
# seed, 64 bars, two transpositions, two mutes) played on the app, every message it sends logged with its tick, and
# the log compared line by line with what RefTool's midi mode writes for the same script (midi_full.midiref: Start,
# the notes and CC of each window of 240 ticks as NoteEventConverter makes them, the clock, in a stable sort by tick).
selfscript tests/equiv/midi_full.midiscript
dumpmidi app/build/scenarios/play_midi/midi_dump.txt
tap PLAY
expect playing 1
# 64 bars at 96 BPM: 160 s from tick 0, which sounds 100 ms after the press; the last note-off is on bar 64's line
wait 161000
expect head 245760
expect tick >245760
cmpmidi tests/equiv/midi_full.midiref
expect midicmp 0
expect midilines 9466
expect sounding 0
expect queued 0
expect dropped 0
expect clocks_out 6144
